    "workload": "build 8 gas/cost array pairs of 200000 elements once, then 1200 punches of the greedy single pass. Half the pairs are feasible (costs drawn from a smaller range than gas) and half are not; both walk the entire array since the algorithm has no early exit, but they differ in how often the tank<0 restart fires, which is the only branch in the loop. NOTE: the bench passes the arrays by reference where the kata takes Vec[i64] by value -- by value would copy 200000 elements per call, which no mirror does and which would swamp the O(n) scan being measured.",
